#if(v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 1) {
It takes more than a minute of persistent shaking to draw her awake. Even upright, she is pale and unsteady, breathing shallowly. Healing spells have their limits; closing flesh is one thing, but restoring drained stamina takes time. She will need at least another full day to shake off the morning's trauma.

We sit with her and lay out everything that took place after Eiden appeared.

When we finish, Kate stares into the shadows of the cave, weighing every word.

"Let me get this straight," she says. "Barry, you traded our lives for a single message."

"That's the deal."

"And we're supposed to deliver it to anyone in robes wearing a brooch shaped like a hawk clutching the sun."

