"And what's the plan for that?" Kate's voice turns sharp. "He bypassed your sleep wards in half a second, and your defenses are sturdier than mine. That single spell would incapacitate the three of us, to say nothing of the rest of his arsenal."

"So we just roll over and run his errands like obedient dogs?"

"Nobody said that. I'm saying we lack the intelligence to construct a viable strategy. Until we uncover a vulnerability in his technique, we should make the most of the reprieve Barry negotiated, however long it lasts."

I catch the phrasing and file it away. The reprieve Barry negotiated. Not "the deal you stumbled into." Not "the mess you made." She framed it as a deliberate tactical move—as if my gambit with Eiden had been a calculated play rather than blind panic dressed up in bravado. Coming from Kate, that is as close to a compliment as I have ever heard.

"Perhaps you're right. Let's hope that window gives us time to find an opening."

He turns to me.

"Barry, did you have any luck locating those medicinal roots for your sister's fever?"

"Not yet," I manage, keeping my face straight. "Still keeping an eye out."

Kate's eyes narrow into a sharp glare.

"Understood," Daren says with an earnest nod. "Let me know if you need an extra pair of eyes."

"Barry," Kate says, stepping between us. "A word outside. In private."

}
choice("Continue", Ch5-Private-truth, v_current_scene = Ch5-Private-truth) if (v_ch2_human_reason == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch5-Private-lie, v_current_scene = Ch5-Private-lie) if (v_ch2_human_reason == 2 || v_ch2_human_reason == 3)


ID: Ch5-Coded
TEXT:

#if(v_ch2_human_reason == 1) {
"It sounds like a coded message," I say. "Something only Eiden and those robed figures would understand, setting a rendezvous or triggering an operation."

"I agree," Daren says. "He wouldn't want messengers deciphering the location or the intent."

"The stillwater wouldn't spare our lives merely to deliver mail," Kate cuts in. "There is always an underlying angle. The phrasing carries teeth. What if they attack the moment we recite the phrase?"

"Steady on," Daren says. "We can't assume hostility from phrasing alone. And our immediate priority should be figuring out how to neutralize Eiden, not obsessing over his errand!"

"And what's the plan for that?" Kate's voice turns sharp. "He bypassed your sleep wards in half a second, and your defenses are sturdier than mine. That single spell would incapacitate the three of us, to say nothing of the rest of his arsenal."

