ID: Ch5-Private-truth
TEXT:

#if(v_ch4_ending != 2) {
She fixes me with an unblinking stare.

"How do you know about the Beacon?" she asks.

"Eiden mentioned you survived it right before he struck Daren. He refused to give specifics—told us to ask you in person. So what is it?"

"It's... complicated."

"Naturally. I don't need your life story. Give me the summary."

"Do you make a habit of prying into everyone's private history?"

"If it were ordinary privacy, I wouldn't press. But it isn't. You've held cards to your chest since the moment we met. The same thing happened just now with the hawk brooches. I'm asking because unanswered questions get groups killed."

"This won't."

"How can you be certain?"

Her gaze shifts sideways, jaw tightening.

"It won't." She draws a sharp breath. "I don't intend to keep it buried forever. It's just... not the time. I promise I will lay it out when the moment comes. If that's all, I'm going back to sleep."

She turns and ducks into the cave. I remain outside, resting my back against the rough stone wall.

Nothing about this tournament adds up. Contestants slaughter each other in the brush, the organizers withhold the basic objectives, and an ancient stillwater wanders the woods looking for amusement. What is he actually after?

}
#if(v_ch4_ending == 2) {
"Do you make a habit of prying into everyone's private history?" she asks.

"If it were ordinary privacy, I wouldn't press. But it isn't. You've held cards to your chest since the moment we met. The same thing happened just now with the hawk brooches. I'm asking because unanswered questions get groups killed."

"This won't."

"How can you be certain?"

Her gaze shifts sideways, jaw tightening.

"It won't." She draws a sharp breath. "I don't intend to keep it buried forever. It's just... not the time. I promise I will lay it out when the moment comes. If that's all, I'm going back to sleep."

She turns and ducks into the cave. I remain outside, resting my back against the rough stone wall.

Nothing about this tournament adds up. Contestants slaughter each other in the brush, the organizers withhold the basic objectives, and an ancient stillwater wanders the woods looking for amusement. What is he actually after?

}
choice("Continue", Ch5-Scream, v_current_scene = Ch5-Scream)


ID: Ch5-Private-lie
TEXT:

#if(v_ch4_ending != 2) {
"Right. Of course," I say, following her outside.

As we pass, Daren catches my eye, winks, and gives me a broad thumbs-up. Leave it to Daren to read romance into an interrogation. His grasp of social cues is truly breathtaking.

Once we clear the entrance, Kate pivots on her heel, fixing me with a hard, unyielding stare.

"You lied to Daren about why you joined this tournament, didn't you?"

"And if I did?"

"Why deceive him? Do you believe he'd treat you as an enemy over the prize? And even if he did, why would a healer like Daren pose a threat to you?"

"Everyone lies. Everyone holds cards back. You're no different. You haven't told Daren a single word about the Beacon of Hope, have you?"

The certainty drains from her expression, replaced by sharp tension.

"What do you know about the Beacon of Hope?"

"Not much. Eiden called you a survivor from that place, but he wouldn't elaborate. Told me to ask you directly. So what is the Beacon of Hope?"

Her jaw tightens.

"It's... complicated."

"Right. See what I mean? You're keeping secrets from him too. How is that any different from what I'm doing?"

"It is different. You should tell Daren the truth. But do as you please. That's all I have to say."

She spins on her heel and marches back into the darkness of the cave.

}
#if(v_ch4_ending == 2) {
