"Everyone lies. Everyone holds cards back. You're no different. You haven't told Daren a single word about the Beacon of Hope, have you?"

"That's not the same thing!"

"How so?"

She holds my gaze for several tight seconds, then lets the question drop unanswered.

"You should tell Daren the truth. But I'm not going to force you. Do as you please. That's all I have to say."

She spins on her heel and marches back into the darkness of the cave.

}
choice("Tell Daren the truth", Ch5-Admit-lie, v_current_scene = Ch5-Admit-lie, v_ch5_admit_lie = 1)
choice("Don't say anything to Daren", Ch5-No-admit, v_current_scene = Ch5-No-admit, v_ch5_admit_lie = 0)


ID: Ch5-Admit-lie
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch5_liar,1)
achievement("Admitted liar",v_ac_ch5_liar)
#if(v_ch2_human_reason == 2) {
Kate has a point. Daren has offered nothing but honesty and protection since we met, and I repaid him with a manufactured excuse. He won't take the confession well, but hearing it from me now is better than letting him discover the deceit on his own.

"Daren, there's something I need to tell you," I say, stepping back into the cave.

Kate, settling onto her bedroll, watches me closely, waiting to see if I follow through.

"Easy, Barry. Conversations opening with those words rarely bring good news."

I exhale slowly.

"I lied to you yesterday about why I came to Varathia. Nobody forced me here. I came of my own free will because I want to win this tournament. Ever since I was a child, I've wanted to become a mage, and the Magium can grant that. I'm sorry for misleading you."

"Oh," Daren says.

His eyes go flat and cold.

"Well. Now I know."

"Now you know."

Kate offers a faint, approving nod from the shadows, but Daren's expression remains stone-still. I leave him to process the revelation and step back toward the open air.

}
#if(v_ch2_human_reason == 3) {
